# build output
/dist/
# ... and the staging the CI build scatters beside it. The release job makes one directory per
# architecture, copies the binary and the installer scripts in, and tars it; the matrix job leaves
# its tarball in the root. All of it is build output, but it sat in the working tree UNTRACKED - so
# from the second architecture onward scripts/buildinfo.sh saw a non-empty `git status` and stamped
# every later binary DIRTY, and the release refused itself over sources that had not changed at all.
# The guard was right about the tree and wrong about what it meant; ignoring build output is what
# makes the dirty flag mean "built from modified source" again.
/wayhop-*-pkg/
/wayhop-*.tar.gz
/bins/
/pkgs/
# local runtime state (created by demo/run) — machine-specific, may hold secrets
/.wrdata/
/profile.json
/profile.json.tmp
/dev-config.json
/dev-config.json.tmp
/servers.json
/servers.json.tmp
/singbox.json
# feed signing PRIVATE keys — the .pub halves ARE committed; the private halves live only in the
# GitHub Actions secrets (WAYHOP_USIGN_SEC / WAYHOP_APK_SEC_PEM) and a LOCAL-ONLY backup
# (%LOCALAPPDATA%\wayhop-keys — never inside a cloud-synced folder). Losing them
# forces a key rotation (every device must re-trust), so keep that local backup.
/packaging/feed/keys/*.sec
/packaging/feed/keys/*.pem

# editor / OS cruft
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Locally-built binaries at the repo root. /dist/ is already ignored, but a plain
# `go build` with no -o drops the executable here, where an `add -A` would commit ~16 MB.
/wayhop.exe
/wayhop
/usigntool.exe
/usigntool

# Redesign-session artefacts. The audit tree is worked in place, so a build, a demo log or a
# scratch probe left at the root would otherwise be swept into a commit.
/wayhop-redesign.exe
/redesign-demo.log
/redesign-demo.err.log
/verify_usage.txt
/rd-wayhop.exe
/rd-wayhop.exe~
/wrscratch.exe
# The demo the UI gates run against. Regenerated from scratch by `node scripts/seed-demo.mjs`,
# which IS tracked, so the seed is reproducible and the 39KB of generated profile state is not
# worth carrying — same reason /profile.json is ignored above.
/rd-demo/
# On Windows `> nul` in a POSIX shell creates a real file instead of discarding, so a redirected
# screenshot lands here as a 100KB PNG named `nul`.
/nul

# Per-session scratch under .claude. The i18n dictionaries and launch config there ARE tracked;
# these are throwaway probe scripts and captures from individual investigations.
.claude/bug-hunt/
.claude/c[0-9][0-9]-*
.claude/c[0-9][0-9]/
.claude/tmp-*
.claude/per-device/
.claude/research/
.claude/routing-check/
.claude/ui-review/
.claude/gemini-review-*.md

# Build backups left by the redesign loop.
/wayhop-redesign.exe~

# scripts/i18n-merge-pending.mjs copies each dictionary beside itself before writing, so a failed
# batch can be put back. Those copies are ~100KB each across fifteen languages and are worthless
# once the merge is verified — but they sit inside a TRACKED directory, so without this line the
# next `git add` on .claude/i18n would carry them in.
.claude/i18n/dicts/*.bak
